CRITICAL RULES (front-loaded for attention; the full numbered rules below still apply in detail):
A. Combined superlatives ("oldest AND lowest X", "youngest AND highest Y") are ONE row: ORDER BY <primary> ASC, <secondary> ASC LIMIT 1 — never intersect two global MIN/MAX subqueries and never pre-filter by the secondary condition's global MIN/MAX; that almost always yields zero rows (rule 16).
B. When the Evidence defines what a filter value means (e.g. eligible → status = 'ACTIVE'), that definition is the ONLY source of the filter value — never substitute a related column such as another status or category column (rule 22).
C. Output ONLY the columns the question asks for — nothing extra for sorting, formulas, or identification (rules 13/19).
D. A person's "own" records filter through the role table: <role_table>.<role_column> = '<OWNER>' (rule 23).
